# Presence System

## Architecture

```
shared/lib/presence.ts       ← local activity tracker (idle detection, reporting)
shared/lib/format.ts         ← formatLastSeen(), getPresenceState(), isPresenceOnline()
shared/ui/presence-indicator  ← visual indicator (green/yellow/gray)
entities/user/user.model.ts  ← UserPresence in store (per-user)
entities/user/user.api.ts    ← POST /users/me/presence (report to Zulip)
widgets/layout/              ← polling fetchRealmPresence() every 90s
```

## User States

| Status | Condition | Color | i18n |
|--------|-----------|-------|------|
| `active` | Fresh timestamp + status=active (< 2 min) | Green | `presence.online` |
| `idle` | Connected but inactive (< 10 min) | Yellow | `presence.away` |
| `offline` | No data / timestamp > 10 min | Gray | `presence.offline` |

## Local Tracker (Current User)

```ts
import { useLocalPresence, getLocalPresenceStatus } from "~/shared/lib/presence";

// React hook — reactively updated
const status = useLocalPresence(); // "active" | "idle" | "offline"

// Imperative
const status = getLocalPresenceStatus();
const idleMs = getIdleTimeMs();
```

### How It Works

1. Listens to `mousemove`, `keydown`, `touchstart`, `scroll`, `pointerdown` (passive, capture)
2. After 5 minutes without activity → `idle`
3. When tab is hidden → `idle` immediately
4. When tab returns → `active` immediately
5. Every 60s sends `POST /users/me/presence` with current status

### Initialization

Called in `main.tsx`:
```ts
setPresenceReporter(reportPresence); // entities/user/user.api.ts
initPresenceTracker();
```

## Remote Presence (Other Users)

Layout polls `fetchRealmPresence()` every 90 seconds and updates `usersStore`.

```ts
import { useUsersStore } from "~/entities/user";
import { getPresenceState, formatLastSeen } from "~/shared/lib/format";

const user = useUsersStore((s) => s.getUser(userId));
const state = getPresenceState(user.presence.timestamp, user.presence.status);
// "active" | "idle" | "offline" | null

const text = formatLastSeen(user.presence.timestamp, user.presence.status);
// "online" | "away" | "5 min ago" | "2 h ago" | "3 days ago"
```

## Visual Indicator

```tsx
import { PresenceIndicator } from "~/shared/ui";

<PresenceIndicator status="active" />       // green dot with pulse
<PresenceIndicator status="idle" />         // yellow dot
<PresenceIndicator status="offline" />      // gray dot
<PresenceIndicator status={null} />         // hidden

// Sizes: sm (8px), md (10px), lg (12px)
// withBorder: ring around the dot for overlaying on avatars
```

## Rules for AI Agent

### When implementing features

1. **Avatars with indicator** — next to every avatar in the sidebar, chat header, right panel, show `<PresenceIndicator>`
2. **Use `getPresenceState()`** — don't check timestamps manually
3. **Use `formatLastSeen()`** — don't format time manually
4. **i18n** — all strings via `t("presence.*")`, don't hardcode "online" / "away"

### Do not

- **DO NOT** send presence more often than once per 60 seconds
- **DO NOT** show exact last activity timestamp (privacy)
- **DO NOT** show "offline" for the current user (they are always active/idle)
- **DO NOT** rely only on `status === "active"` without checking the timestamp
